[CENTER]
[SIZE=6][B][COLOR=#00D2FF]CustomMusic Documentation & Admin Guide[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
[SIZE=3]Complete setup instructions, song importing guide, configuration reference, and developer API.[/SIZE]
[/CENTER]

[HR][/HR]

[SIZE=5][B][COLOR=#00D2FF]1. Installation[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
[LIST=1]
[*]Download the latest [B]CustomMusic.jar[/B] release.
[*]Place the file into your server's [B]plugins/[/B] directory.
[*](Optional) Ensure [B]Vault[/B] (with an economy plugin like EssentialsX) and [B]PlaceholderAPI[/B] are installed.
[*]Restart your server. CustomMusic will automatically generate configuration files, database tables, and extract 24 bundled popular songs into [B]plugins/CustomMusic/songs/[/B].
[/LIST]

[HR][/HR]

[SIZE=5][B][COLOR=#00D2FF]2. Adding Custom NBS Songs[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
CustomMusic supports all Note Block Studio (.nbs) files.
[LIST=1]
[*]Drop your [B].nbs[/B] files into [B]plugins/CustomMusic/songs/[/B].
[*]Ensure file names do not contain special characters (e.g., [I]my_song.nbs[/I]).
[*]In-game or in console, execute [B]/cm scan[/B].
[*]The plugin will instantly index the files and make them available in the Catalog and Radio rotation!
[*]Alternatively, register songs with a specific price using:
[CODE]/cm add <song_id> <price> <Display Song Name>[/CODE]
[/LIST]

[HR][/HR]

[SIZE=5][B][COLOR=#00D2FF]3. Adding Custom Resource Pack Sounds (.ogg)[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
If you have a server resource pack with custom music disc tracks, you can add them to [B]config.yml[/B]:
[CODE=yaml]
custom_ogg_tracks:
  epic_track:
    sound: "minecraft:music_disc.custom_one"
    length: 180
    title: "<gold>Epic Adventure Theme</gold>"
    price: 250.0
    permission: ""
[/CODE]
After adding, run [B]/cm reload[/B] to load the new custom tracks.

[HR][/HR]

[SIZE=5][B][COLOR=#00D2FF]4. Configuration Breakdown[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]

[B]config.yml:[/B]
[LIST]
[*][B]general.volume_multiplier:[/B] Master volume scaler (default: 1.0).
[*][B]general.volume_step:[/B] Percentage change per click in volume controls (default: 5).
[*][B]radio.enabled:[/B] Enables or disables the global 24/7 radio broadcaster.
[*][B]radio.pause_between_tracks_seconds:[/B] Intermission length between radio songs.
[*][B]displays.boss_bar_enabled:[/B] Show BossBar during playback with track duration.
[*][B]displays.action_bar_enabled:[/B] Show ActionBar during playback.
[*][B]disco_floor.palette:[/B] List of concrete/block materials cycled in dance floor mode.
[*][B]portable_companion.sneak_interact:[/B] Allows picking up music boxes with Shift + Right Click.
[/LIST]

[HR][/HR]

[SIZE=5][B][COLOR=#00D2FF]5. Developer API[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
CustomMusic provides a static API facade for third-party plugins:

[CODE=java]
import com.lino.custommusic.api.CustomMusicAPI;
import com.lino.custommusic.model.MusicBox;

// Play a registered song at a location
CustomMusicAPI.playSongAt(location, "megalovania", 80);

// Retrieve active companion box for a player
Optional<MusicBox> companion = CustomMusicAPI.getCompanionBox(player);
companion.ifPresent(box -> {
    box.setVolume(100);
});
[/CODE]

[HR][/HR]

